# CLI Prompt Symbol Rendering
## Overview
The CLI prompts use Unicode symbols for beautiful, modern rendering across all platforms including Git Bash on Windows.
## Symbol Set
All prompts use the following Unicode symbols:
```
Step Active:       ◆
Step Submit:       ◇
Bar Start:         ┌
Bar:               │
Bar End:           └
Radio Active:      ●
Radio Inactive:    ○
Checkbox Active:   ◻
Checkbox Selected: ◼
Password Mask:     •
```
## Platform Support
These Unicode symbols render correctly on:
- ✅ Git Bash (MINGW64) on Windows
- ✅ Windows Terminal
- ✅ ConEmu
- ✅ Unix/Linux/macOS terminals
- ✅ Modern terminal emulators
## Cursor Behavior
The cursor is automatically hidden during prompt interaction for a cleaner experience:
- Hidden when prompts are active
- Restored when prompts complete (submit, cancel, or error)
- Applies to all prompt types: select, multiselect, input, password, confirm
- Also applies to spinner and progress bar animations
## Testing
Run the test example to see the symbols in your terminal:
```bash
cargo run --example test_symbols --manifest-path crates/cli/Cargo.toml
```
## Implementation Details
The symbol system is implemented in `crates/cli/src/prompts/mod.rs`:
- `Symbols` struct: Holds all symbol definitions
- `SYMBOLS`: Global symbol set (always Unicode)
- Cursor hiding: Implemented in `PromptInteraction::interact()`
All prompt components automatically use the Unicode symbol set and hide the cursor during interaction.
## Benefits
- **Beautiful rendering**: Consistent Unicode symbols across all platforms
- **Git Bash support**: Works perfectly in Git Bash on Windows
- **Clean interface**: Cursor hidden during interaction
- **Professional appearance**: Modern CLI aesthetic
- **No configuration**: Just works out of the box